{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: implement conservative, inspectable Tailapp source and projection upgrades that preserve custom work.","body":{"conditions":"Depends on safe binary upgrades. At a reviewed exact head, record durable provenance for each first-party bundle installation: built-in origin, bundle name, installed release/baseline source digest, and current-source comparison basis. Provide a machine-readable upgrade plan that classifies every app as user-generated, pristine built-in, or modified built-in and separately reports runtime compatibility. Generated and modified apps are never rewritten, merged, activated, or reset automatically; modified built-ins receive an intelligible three-way upstream/current/baseline diff or equivalent conflict report. --apply-safe may update only a pristine built-in whose release metadata explicitly certifies continuation safety, after validation and optimistic-revision checks. Schema or semantic changes requiring reset, and every non-certified change, require explicit app selection and confirmation; never infer safety from schema shape alone. Before any reset or nontrivial source/projection change, require a coherent user-selected backup location with capacity/error handling and a documented restore path. Provide explicit continue/reset commands, protect user drafts, test every classification and failed/rollback path, and document that normal binary upgrades leave custom apps and data untouched.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}